  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} f(x)=a \\ln 2 \\ln 3 \\\\ & \\lim _{n \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{72^x-9^x-8^x+1}{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{1+\\cos x}}=\\lim _{x \\rightarrow 0} \\frac{\\left(8^x-1\\right)\\left(9^x-1\\right)}{\\sqrt{2}-\\sqrt{1+\\cos x}} \\\\ & \\lim _{n \\rightarrow 0}\\left(\\frac{8^x-1}{x}\\right)\\left(\\frac{9^x-1}{x}\\right)\\left(\\frac{x^2}{1-\\cos x}\\right)(\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{1+\\cos x}) \\\\ & \\therefore \\ln 8 \\times \\ln 9 \\times 2 \\times 2 \\sqrt{2}=24 \\sqrt{2} \\ln 2 \\ln 3 \\\\ & \\therefore a=24 \\sqrt{2}, a^2=576 \\times 2=1152\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
